without right variables. However, we can check if there exists any assignment for e and g that can satisfy those constraints given b and d. But we don't have e and g values yet.\n\nThus, perhaps the left component tuple enumeration is a specific assignment for a,b,c,d that was previously provided (maybe in a prior message not shown). Since we don't have it, we need to request it? But the instruction says \"Use CHALLENGE only if you found a specific issue; otherwise REPORT_EVIDENCE with supported or underdetermined.\" So we need to either report that the left component tuple enumeration is supported (i.e., consistent) or underdetermined (i.e., insufficient info). Since we don't have the enumeration, we cannot verify it. So we might need to report underdetermined.\n\nBut the envelope template includes \"assessment\": \"supported\". That seems to assume we are supporting the enumeration. But we don't know the enumeration. However, perhaps the left component tuple enumeration is implied by the constraints and domain, i.e., we need to enumerate all possible tuples for a,b,c,d that satisfy c1-c4. That enumeration could be considered the \"left component tuple enumeration\". Then we need to check that enumeration against the public constraints (including cross constraints). So we need to compute all possible assignments for a,b,c,d that satisfy c1-c4. Then we need to see if those assignments can be extended to full assignments for all variables (including e,f,g,h) that satisfy all constraints. If there exists at least one full assignment for each left tuple, then the enumeration is supported. If not, then it's underdetermined (i.e., some left tuples cannot be extended). Or maybe we need to produce a candidate tuple (full assignment) as evidence.\n\nThe role task says \"Edit assessment, basis_refs, and candidate tuples only.\" So we need to produce a report with assessment (supported/underdetermined) and basis_refs (list of constraints we used). Also candidate tuples (maybe