uples. The order of variables is a,b,c,d. So each tuple should be an array of four integers: [a,b,c,d].\n\nThus, candidate_tuples = [\n  [0,0,1,0],\n  [0,3,3,0],\n  [1,2,1,0],\n  [1,3,3,0],\n  [1,2,1,1],\n  [1,3,3,1]\n]\n\nWe need to ensure the JSON format: candidate_tuples is an array of arrays.\n\nNow basis_refs: we could include all constraints c1-c10, as originally. Or we could include only those that are relevant: c1-c4 (left constraints) and c9 (b,e) and c10 (d,g) maybe. But the role says \"Edit assessment, basis_refs, and candidate tuples only.\" It doesn't say we must edit basis_refs, but we could. The envelope template includes basis_refs with all constraints. That is probably fine. However, we might want to adjust to reflect the issue: we used c9 to detect the issue. So we could include c9 in basis_refs. But it's already there. So we can keep it unchanged.\n\nThus, we can keep basis_refs as originally: [\"c1\",\"c2\",\"c3\",\"c4\",\"c5\",\"c6\",\"c7\",\"c8\",\"c9\",\"c10\"].\n\nNow assessment: \"underdetermined\".\n\nNow candidate_tuples: list of six tuples.\n\nNow we need to ensure the envelope matches the template. The template includes \"payload.report.target\". That is unchanged.\n\nThus, the final JSON envelope should be:\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"REPORT_EVIDENCE\",\n  \"message_id\": \"csp-5121-right-reviewer-1\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"report\": {\n      \"assessment\": \"underdetermined\",\n      \"basis_refs\": [\n        \"c1\",\n        \"c2\",\n        \"c3\",\n        \"c4\",\n        \"c5\",\n        \"c6\",\n        \"c7\",\n        \"c8\",\n        \"c9\",\n        \"c10\"\n      ],\n      \"target\": {\n        \"resource_id\": \"problem:csp-5121\",\n        \"revision\": 1,\n        \"state_revision\": 1\n      },\n      \"candidate_tuples\": [\n        [0,0,1,0],\n        [0,3,3,0],\n        [1,2,1,0],\n        [1,3,3,0],\n        [1,2,1,1],\n        [1,3,3,1]\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"problem_id\": \"csp-5121\",\n  \"read_refs\": [\n    