check each tuple against c1-c4.\n\nWe already checked each. All good.\n\nNow we need to ensure that the candidate tuples are enumerated in variable order (a,b,c,d). Yes.\n\nNow we need to ensure that the assessment is \"underdetermined\". The left component tuple enumeration is underdetermined because some left tuples cannot be extended to a full solution (L2). So assessment is underdetermined.\n\nNow basis_refs: we could include all constraints, but we might want to include only those used to identify the issue. However, the role says \"Edit assessment, basis_refs, and candidate tuples only.\" It doesn't require us to change basis_refs. So we can keep them as originally. But the original basis_refs includes all constraints. That is fine.\n\nNow we need to ensure that the envelope's message_id matches the template: \"csp-5121-right-reviewer-1\". Yes.\n\nNow we need to ensure that the \"payload.report.target\" matches the template: resource_id, revision, state_revision. Yes.\n\nNow we need to ensure that the \"read_refs\" matches the template: one entry with resource_id, revision, state_revision. Yes.\n\nNow we need to ensure that the \"recipients\" list includes \"shared-integrator\". Yes.\n\nNow we need to ensure that the \"reply_to\" is null. Yes.\n\nNow we need to ensure that the \"schema_version\" is 1. Yes.\n\nNow we need to ensure that the \"sender\" is \"right-reviewer\". Yes.\n\nNow we need to ensure that we didn't add any extra fields like \"candidate_tuples\" that are not in the template. The role says we need to edit candidate tuples, so we must add it. The envelope template didn't include it, but we need to add it. The user said \"Return exactly one JSON protocol envelope matching the supplied template; no prose outside JSON.\" This is ambiguous: do we need to match exactly the keys, or can we add fields? Usually, \"matching the supplied template\" means the envelope should follow the structure of the template, but we can fill in missing fields. However,